32.m:
The sages said:
The sun god has been declared by you to be without qualities and eternal;
yet we have heard from your words that he was born again in twelve ways.

Brahmā said:
Then the lord Vibhāvasu emerged from that splendour;
the sun was seen then by her, resembling molten copper, the lord.

Brahmā said:
Having spoken thus, the radiant lord disappeared;
and having attained all that she desired, she ceased her austerities.

35.m:
The king of mountains said:
“Lord, I do not disregard brāhmaṇas, who are gods on earth;
but hear what was previously resolved, O high-minded one!

The goddess said:
“O lord of alligators, tell me quickly what is not condemned by the virtuous;
that is done, there is no doubt about this, because brāhmaṇas are dear to me.”

